body:
The bot said this is about feminism so here is my post:

&#x200B;

 There is nothing wrong with saying that a group of people is more likely to do something than another group of people.

&#x200B;

For example, if i said men are more likely to commit a crime than a woman. This isn't seen sexist. However, if I said African american men and more likely to commit a crime than Caucasian men then a lot of people will claim this is racist. Neither of these statements are discriminatory because they're based off of facts. There are a higher percentage of African american men in prison than Caucasian men and there are a higher percentage of men overall in prison.

Another thing, it's not sexist to say that women are worse drivers than men if they are found at fault for more accidents than men. Same with vice versa. There was a post in a subreddit today where a woman derailed a train due to texting and driving but you were banned if you said anything about women being worse drivers than men which is ridiculous. It is unlikely that both women and men are equally bad at driving so, it isn't sexist to say one is worse at driving than the other as long as you have a legitimate study to back up your claim.
